# Initial geometry for subduction.cfg (mat.phase_change_option 3),
# 400 km x 160 km. An oceanic-crust slab
# (material 0) is already in the mantle, and the serpentinization grid reads its
# crust. Mantle just above the slab top (9-11, the mantle-wedge side) turns
# into serpentinite, and the slab crust turns into eclogite at depth. No region
# holds serpentinite (4) or eclogite (5): only the phase changes make them.
#
# The slab is 7 km thick. It starts at the trench (x = 125-139 km, z = -9 km)
# and dips 30 deg to its end at z = -34 to -40 km, cut normal to the dip. A
# 10 km wide halo of refined mantle (region 3) wraps the slab, so the mesh
# resolves the serpentinite layer above the slab top.
#
# Schematic (not to scale):
#
#  0------------------------------------------7  z = 0: top, free surface
#  1------------------------------------------6  z = -2 km: sediment / crust
#  2----12--8=====9--13-----------------------5  z = -9 km: crust / mantle
#  |      \  \  0  \   \                      |
#  |       \  10----11   15                   |  10-11: slab end, normal to the dip
#  |        \         \ /                     |  12-14: halo below the slab
#  |         14-------/                       |  13-15: halo above the slab
#  |                                          |
#  3------------------------------------------4  z = -160 km: bottom

#### node coordinates ####
# npoints ndims 0 0
  16      2     0 0
# i    xi       zi
  0        0.00        0.00
  1        0.00    -2000.00    # sediment / crust, left wall
  2        0.00    -9000.00    # crust / mantle, left wall
  3        0.00  -160000.00
  4   400000.00  -160000.00
  5   400000.00    -9000.00    # crust / mantle, right wall
  6   400000.00    -2000.00    # sediment / crust, right wall
  7   400000.00        0.00
  8   125000.00    -9000.00    # slab base at the trench
  9   139000.00    -9000.00    # slab top at the trench
 10   178690.00   -40000.00    # slab base end
 11   182190.00   -33937.82    # slab top end (7 km normal to the dip)
 12   104996.42    -9000.00    # halo below the slab, at z = -9 km
 13   158996.42    -9000.00    # halo above the slab, at z = -9 km
 14   182350.25   -53660.25    # halo corner below the slab end
 15   195850.25   -30277.57    # halo corner above the slab end
#### segments ####
# nsegments 1
  20        1
# j  pj0  pj1  bdry_flag
  0   0   1    1    # 1: left (x0)
  1   1   2    1
  2   2   3    1
  3   3   4   16    # 16: bottom (z0)
  4   4   5    2    # 2: right (x1)
  5   5   6    2
  6   6   7    2
  7   7   0   32    # 32: top (z1)
  8   1   6    0    # 0: not a boundary
  9   2  12    0
 10  12   8    0
 11   8   9    0
 12   9  13    0
 13  13   5    0
 14   8  10    0
 15  10  11    0
 16  11   9    0
 17  12  14    0
 18  14  15    0
 19  15  13    0
#### holes, must be 0 ####
0
#### regions ####
# nregions
  5
# k  xk    zk   mattype  size (max. element area, m^2)
  0 200000 -1000 3  4e+06  # sediment, z = 0 to -2 km
  1 200000 -7000 0  8e+06  # oceanic crust, z = -2 to -9 km
  2 156220 -22984 0  8e+06  # slab (oceanic crust)
  3 149345 -28830 2  1e+07  # refined mantle halo around the slab
  4 300000 -100000 2  1e+09  # mantle, coarse
